WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm just so used to being
attacked for everything I say,

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.637
it's like at this
point I'm like,

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.006
all right, you know,
what are you gonna do?

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.041 align:start size:81% position:19%
Are you gonna call
me a mean name?

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.509
What would that feel like?

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.977
What would it feel
like to see myself

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.546
called something horrible on
every newspaper in the country?

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:14.948
Oh, wait, I've done that.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.517
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin and
this is the Rubin Report.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.426 align:start position:0% line:0%
As always guys make sure you're
subscribed to our channel

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:29.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
and resubscribe when
YouTube unsubscribes you.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.966
And joining me today is
a bestselling author,

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.534
a TV host, a journalist,

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:38.905
a mother, a dog lover, and
a newly minted podcaster.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.674
Megan Kelly, welcome
to the Rubin Report.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.209
- Hey, so good to be with you.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.980
- A newly minted
podcaster Megan,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.850 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're dipping your
toes in some new waters.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're gonna talk
about everything, but
let's start there.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.488 align:start size:81% position:19%
You're getting
back in the fight.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.322
What are you, nuts?

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.091
- You know, I'm excited.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.427 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Like I thought when I left
NBC that I would just sort of,

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.395 line:0%
maybe this could be my new life.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.098 line:0%
I would just take it easy and
I would take care of my kids,

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:88% position:13%
which was very
enjoyable and remain so,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause they're good
ages right now.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, maybe I'd
be like a lady of leisure,

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:12.705
see how that went.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.574
And then I tuned
out from the news,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.509
which was helpful.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.478
And then, you know, bit by bit,

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.779
I started to pull me back in

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.915
and I started to read
more and more and more

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.250
and then all hell broke
loose in our country.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.221 align:start size:97% position:3%
And like the culture wars
really just make my head spin.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.323
And the one thing
that really made me

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.226 align:start size:97% position:3%
wanna get off the couch over
the time that I had off,

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.595
was the movie, "No Safe Spaces.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:40.600 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I, I was glued to my
chair watching it and I cried.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.002
It was, and I thought, this is,

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.871
I have to get back out there.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.273
They're just, there
aren't enough people

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are saying the things
that need to be said.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.678
There's too many people
who are being silenced

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.546
just for having a
dissenting voice,

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:56.316
a reasonable but
dissenting voice.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start position:0%
And if you have the opportunity
to get to a microphone

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:01.821 align:start size:97% position:3%
and have those discussions,
you better do it.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.655
So here I am.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.126
- So since I was in
"No Safe Spaces",

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:09.362
can I fully credit myself
for bringing Megan Kelly

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.430
back into the fight?

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.232
Is that, is that fair?

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.467
- You and Adam and Dennis

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.035
and Ben and Mark Joseph,

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.538
the producer, who I came
to know over the years.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.939
And he's just,

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.775 align:start size:97% position:3%
he's so unsung as an
amazing filmmaker, you know,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.378
he's doing in Hollywood,
what nobody else is doing,

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.882 align:start position:0%
which is trying to shed a light
on some conservative causes

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:32.819 line:0%
some this even center
or center right issues.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.387 line:0%
And I'll just give you
one quick example, Dave,

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.724 line:0%
when I had my show on NBC,
he called me up and he said,

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.660
I have Susette Kelo from
Kelo versus Connecticut.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, the case that
went all the way up

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.396
to the Supreme court.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it was an
eminent domain case.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.366
Does the state have the ability

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.401
to grab her little pink house,

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.869
even though she doesn't
want them to have it

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.938
under eminent domain,
like they need it.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:56.776
And she, she, everybody
on my team was like,

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.145
Oh, huh, huh, right?

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.247
They weren't into it and
I was like, I want her.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:04.184 align:start size:88% position:13%
So we put her on, and
Mark was the connection.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.519 align:start size:97% position:3%
It was the highest rated
segment we had the entire time

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.021
on NBC, by far.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:11.558
It was like that guy is
tapping into something.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:14.827
You know, Americans want more
stories about the little guy.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
They don't, they
don't live and breathe

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.598
Hollywood celebrities.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:22.435 align:start size:97% position:3%
And anyway, I love Mark
Joseph and I love that movie.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.170 align:start size:84% position:16%
And if your audience
has not seen it,

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:28.208
it's available now online and
it is so worth your two hours.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.176
- Yeah, well,

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.212 align:start size:88% position:13%
you've also been
through your own version

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.747 align:start size:88% position:13%
of what we were talking
about in the movie,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:38.484
which is the cancel thing and
the mob and all that stuff.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.820
But you know, we've gotten to
know each other a little bit

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.155
in the last year,

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.324
so I didn't have to
do major research

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.558
to talk to you right now,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.860
but I did scribble down
a couple things here.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.362
And one of them
that I wrote down

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:50.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
was that how you're
getting back into the fight

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:53.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's sorta like the
mafia pulling you back in.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you just said you were
sort of reeled back in

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.370
by this thing.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.772
And is that sort of how
you feel about the news,

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.342
like that you love it,

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.744 align:start size:84% position:16%
but then also you
kind of need to escape

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:08.281
and then it just sucks
you back in either way?

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.450
- Yes, because the
thing for me is,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.652
I have never been
a political person.

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:15.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I was never jazzed
up just by politics.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:16.923
You know what I mean?

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.324 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like I used to look
at Charles Krauthammer

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.126 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the way he was
just, he loved politics

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.628
and he wrote about it,

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:23.196
the way, like it was the
most important thing ever.

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.864
And as somebody who
was raised, sort of,

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.133
non-ideological not even
watching the evening news,

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.501
we watched the Jeffersons.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.703 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was like, you
know, I don't know.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.972
I like covering the news,

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:37.076
And I like talking
about politics to
the extent it's news,

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.012 align:start size:84% position:16%
but not just beating
up politicians

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:42.282
and battering around issues
just to make an hour on TV.

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.584
And what happened to me was,

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.185
I started watching more
and more of the news,

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.254
and of course we had political
fights going left and right.

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:49.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was not so
interested in getting back

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
to cover the latest fight
between George Conway

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.327
and president Trump at all.

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:57.664 align:start size:97% position:3%
But the culture wars, what's
happening in our society,

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.898
what's happening legally,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.133
I mean, right now it's like,

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.534
this is right in my wheelhouse.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.703
Everything is happening
with the Supreme Court.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:07.340
And just more and more like
the erosion of our freedoms,

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.342 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is, you know, I
practiced law for 10 years.

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:14.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's, it's a noble
cause for which to fight

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.116
and you'll get called names
and you'll get beaten up

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.851
and it'll be very brutal,

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.087 align:start size:97% position:3%
but there are so many
people who are on your side

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.256
and I'm not saying you're
against all the things

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:24.757
that you're talking about,

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.760
but you're talking about
them, talking about them.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.295 align:start size:88% position:13%
I feel like that,
that's what inspired me

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:30.830
to get back out here.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.099 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Let's talk about
the Jeffersons.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.133
- Yeah.
- George-

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.736 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Louise.
- George would probably,

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:39.472
George would probably
be a Republican, right?

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like he was a successful-
- Probably.

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:44.110
- Business owner, you know,

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.978
moved on up to the East side.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.147
He'd probably be a Republican.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.483 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You're probably right,
he did build that.

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:53.219
Although I don't know,
Marla Gibbs, the maid.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.754
I don't, she was my favorite.

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:57.190
I'm not sure, she'd probably
give him a hard time for it.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.024
- Oh, she would.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.125
That was Florence,

00:05:59.125 --> 00:05:59.926 align:start size:84% position:16%
she would definitely-
- Florence.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:00.660
- Give him a hard time.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.763 align:start size:84% position:16%
Speaking of, speaking
of New York city,

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.666
you are actually in New
York city right now.

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:10.970
What the hell is going on
in New York city right now?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.372
- Oh my God, it's like,

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.175
you know, to me, it's sad
because I've lived here,

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:19.445
I mean, off and on, I've
lived here for 15, 17 years

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:22.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we moved to
the Upper West side

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:24.283 align:start size:84% position:16%
because it had become
a neighborhood.

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:28.020 align:start position:0%
It had become a safe place
where you could raise your kids

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.123
and you could stroll
down the sidewalks

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.924 align:start size:84% position:16%
and with good
schools and you know,

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:34.093 align:start size:88% position:13%
cute little bodegas
where you could just go

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:36.362
and get a bagel, whatever.

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:40.299 align:start size:88% position:13%
And, and in like a year,
our mayor ruined it.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.335 align:start size:97% position:3%
He, I mean, you really
have to tip your hat to him

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.604
because it's not easy
to wreck New York,

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:45.838
but he did it.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.140
And I mean, we're
gonna come back,

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.674
I don't believe for one second,

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:52.211
that New Yorkers are gonna
lie down and stay lying down.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.447 align:start size:84% position:16%
But boy, this mayor's
given us quite a,

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:56.916
quite a fight 'cause the
city is totally different

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.485
than it was just before
I left for quarantine.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.953
I mean, it's depressing.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.755 align:start size:97% position:3%
It looks like 1970s New York,
where I came all the time

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:04.891
'cause my nana lived here.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:06.325
It's like, it's not even just,

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:08.661 align:start size:97% position:3%
there is obviously a
massive homeless problem on,

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.463
on the Upper West side in
particular where I live,

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:13.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he moved, he
built three hotels up here

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:16.569 align:start size:84% position:16%
with homeless people,
without any plan.

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.172 align:start size:84% position:16%
1/3 of them were
convicted pedophiles.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.940
And it's like, well, you know,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.675
maybe we could use
a heads up on that,

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:25.511
a plan on how to deal with it.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:26.379
No, he didn't.

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:28.881
It's like walking
down the street

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:32.051
and just hearing
so much profanity,

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
which I like a good swear
just as much as anybody else,

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:36.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I try not to drop
them in front of my kids,

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:37.356
in front of my seven year old,

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.192
but the vulgarity too Dave,

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:41.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's just like, I'm gonna
take the F and this,

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:43.329 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I'm gonna do this
to you, you know,

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.364
somebody in the cell
phone talking, like,

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:50.036
I'm so sad about
it, I feel loss.

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:52.705
- Yeah, you know, I used
to live on the Upper West

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:55.408 align:start size:97% position:3%
and when I've gone back over
the last couple of years,

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.210
every time I go back,

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.912 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm like, hi, it's a little
worse than last time.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:01.447
A little worse than last time.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.649
And now I haven't been
back since lockdown,

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:06.919
but I told you my sister
and her husband and kids,

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.120
they got out of there.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.623 align:start size:88% position:13%
And it's like, what
kind of future does the,

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:11.891
does the city have?

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:14.260
Do you think people
make the connection

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.829
between what's happening,
like on the ground there

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:19.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the fact that
de Blasio's policies

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.200 align:start size:97% position:3%
are actually what cause it?
- Oh, yes.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.702
- Yeah, you think they do?

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:24.203
- Hundred percent.

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:26.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has such a low approval
rate here in Manhattan.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:27.807
It's under 25%, I think,

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:29.609
according to the
latest poll I saw.

00:08:29.609 --> 00:08:31.210 align:start size:81% position:19%
The Democrats have
turned on him,

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.679 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Republicans have
never been a fan.

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:36.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
I remember having
him on my show on Fox

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:39.285
when he was running, and he
was like last in the poll.

00:08:39.285 --> 00:08:40.753
This is back when Anthony Wiener

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:43.956 align:start position:0%
was supposed to win that mayoral
race, don't get me started.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:47.393
And, and I remember
saying city advocate,

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.594
what the hell is that?

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.129 align:start size:88% position:13%
Nobody ever heard of
you, you have no chance.

00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:52.765
And he was like, 'Oh, I got
a chance, I could do it."

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.100
Like, what do you do
with city advocate,

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.334
I still don't understand.

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:58.538 align:start size:81% position:19%
But I do know now,
he and his wife

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:00.039
are talking about, you know,

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:01.908
layoffs and furloughs.

00:09:01.908 --> 00:09:05.711
And yet his wife still
has her $140,000 a year

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:07.179
speech writer.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:09.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's got her videographer
following her around,

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:11.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
while the trash
bins are overflowing

00:09:11.751 --> 00:09:12.885
on the streets of New York.

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:14.921 align:start size:84% position:16%
The restaurant
owners are suffering.

00:09:14.921 --> 00:09:18.024 align:start position:0%
These mom pop shops, which were
already suffering under him

00:09:18.024 --> 00:09:20.960
have now gone out of business
with no hope of coming back.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.162
So, you know, I hope she
gives a really good speech,

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:25.464
because we're all paying for it.

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:26.666
- Yeah, exactly.

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:27.934 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you mentioned
that the culture war

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:30.236 align:start size:88% position:13%
is partly what's, what's
bringing you back.

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:34.740
And I remember watching you on,
on Fox, you know, years ago.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.543
And what I liked
about you was that,

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:39.011
well, you're just, first off,

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:40.646
some people just know how
to talk to the camera.

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like you just know how
to do it first off.

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:44.317
Was that just always
very natural to you

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:46.686
that you could just be
yourself just like that?

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.989
- No, no, I would not say that.

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:52.158 align:start position:0%
I mean, if you go back and look
at some of my earliest hits

00:09:52.158 --> 00:09:56.329 align:start size:97% position:3%
on Fox and I was on ABC
local, in DC prior to that,

00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:59.298 align:start size:97% position:3%
they're very stilted, they're,
they're pretty stilted.

00:09:59.298 --> 00:10:02.735
I, you know, very, right?

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:06.472 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I always say about
television, it's like typing.

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:09.809 align:start size:97% position:3%
The more you do, the better
you get, the smoother you get.

00:10:09.809 --> 00:10:11.844
But you know, you cannot
get the 70 words a minute

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:14.180
without doing 20, 30, 40.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.681
So I always tell
the young people

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:18.050
who are coming up behind me,
like who wanna be good on TV,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:18.985
Just practice.

00:10:18.985 --> 00:10:20.720
Just say yes to every hit.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.988
There's nothing
that's below you,

00:10:21.988 --> 00:10:23.923
do it and do it often,

00:10:23.923 --> 00:10:25.391
do it even when you
don't wanna do it.

00:10:25.391 --> 00:10:28.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then one day you wake
up and it's not hard.

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:29.895
- Yeah, it's weird, I
look back and I'm like,

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:32.398 align:start size:97% position:3%
man, 20 years ago, when I
was like a struggling comic,

00:10:32.398 --> 00:10:36.268
I was doing, you know, 4:00 AM
radio hits, and it was like,

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:38.270
I was like willing to
absolutely do anything.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:39.972 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I look back and I'm
like, why was I doing that?

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:43.309 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I, I guess maybe it
worked at some level, right?

00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:45.011
- Yeah, it ships in the bank.

00:10:45.011 --> 00:10:47.113
And honestly, even
just the exercise

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:48.514 align:start size:81% position:19%
of getting on your
feet, you know,

00:10:48.514 --> 00:10:51.117 align:start position:0%
like comics have that
experience, which is so helpful.

00:10:51.117 --> 00:10:54.086
And I, as a lawyer had that
as well, which was helpful.

00:10:54.086 --> 00:10:55.755 align:start size:84% position:16%
But like, you gotta
keep doing it.

00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:57.423 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's a muscle
that needs exercise.

00:10:57.423 --> 00:11:00.393 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like getting up there,
making your point.

00:11:00.393 --> 00:11:02.294 line:0%
I used to practice
on a little phone,

00:11:02.294 --> 00:11:04.296 line:0%
like I'm looking into right now.

00:11:04.296 --> 00:11:07.933 line:0%
And I would pretend to do
a television hit, you know,

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:10.403
like there was a fire
down on 54th today,

00:11:10.403 --> 00:11:12.905
which is made up
news, fake news.

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:15.775
And my, my rule for myself was,

00:11:15.775 --> 00:11:18.811
I couldn't stop,
so no matter what,

00:11:18.811 --> 00:11:23.716
if I stumble, I have to do
60 seconds on the fake fire.

00:11:23.716 --> 00:11:25.718
And it was very helpful because

00:11:25.718 --> 00:11:28.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
usually you can stop
and you can have a redo.

00:11:28.888 --> 00:11:30.089
And as you know,
in live television,

00:11:30.089 --> 00:11:31.257
you cannot.

00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:33.993
- All right, let's see how
seasoned you are right now.

00:11:33.993 --> 00:11:36.028
Give me 60 seconds
on that fake fire.

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:38.197
I think it's on
62nd on West End.

00:11:39.598 --> 00:11:42.568 align:start size:97% position:3%
- "On 62nd on West End,
oh, it came to a halt today

00:11:42.568 --> 00:11:44.937
as firetruck came to the
scene within two minutes

00:11:44.937 --> 00:11:46.472
of the first 911 call.

00:11:46.472 --> 00:11:48.607
The blaze turned into
a four alarm fire,

00:11:48.607 --> 00:11:53.012
putting lives at risk, yet the
FDNY did what it always does,

00:11:53.012 --> 00:11:55.815 align:start size:88% position:13%
saved lives and
protected the community.

00:11:55.815 --> 00:11:57.483
More as we get it, back to you."

00:11:58.651 --> 00:12:00.486 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Oh my God, a
true professional.

00:12:00.486 --> 00:12:02.354
You haven't lost it,
you haven't lost it.

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:03.789
- Thank you.
- So anyway,

00:12:03.789 --> 00:12:05.891 align:start size:97% position:3%
so I remember truly, I
remember watching you on Fox

00:12:05.891 --> 00:12:08.394
and it was like, you had
that thing with the camera,

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:10.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also I think what
you said before is right.

00:12:10.096 --> 00:12:11.831 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like you didn't
strike me as someone

00:12:11.831 --> 00:12:14.133
that was consumed by
the political thing.

00:12:14.133 --> 00:12:16.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
And yet now it
seems like everyone,

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:19.972
not just people in the
world that we're in,

00:12:19.972 --> 00:12:23.042 align:start size:84% position:16%
everyone, everywhere,
sports world,

00:12:23.042 --> 00:12:26.312 align:start size:84% position:16%
fashion world, doesn't
matter what world.

00:12:26.312 --> 00:12:28.247
You could be a shoe shiner,

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:30.082
you could be a, you know,

00:12:30.082 --> 00:12:31.517
selling, you can be
working at Petco.

00:12:31.517 --> 00:12:32.752
It doesn't matter what it is.

00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:35.855
Everything is freaking
political right now.

00:12:35.855 --> 00:12:38.824
I know you kind of see
that as much of a danger

00:12:38.824 --> 00:12:40.459
as I do, right?

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:41.293 align:start size:72% position:28%
That sort of-
- Yeah,

00:12:41.293 --> 00:12:42.128
it's my worst nightmare.

00:12:43.262 --> 00:12:45.531 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's my worst nightmare
because what I love

00:12:45.531 --> 00:12:47.133
and one of the reasons
I love practicing law,

00:12:47.133 --> 00:12:49.502
was debating issues.

00:12:49.502 --> 00:12:51.270
I like to be persuaded.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.773 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'd love to be told
that I'm wrong,

00:12:53.773 --> 00:12:55.441 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then be brought
over to the other side.

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:56.675
I know you do too,

00:12:57.943 --> 00:12:59.645 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I'm open
minded to being wrong.

00:12:59.645 --> 00:13:01.480 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, I always say,
I'm a learn it all,

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:02.381
not a know it all.

00:13:03.749 --> 00:13:06.352 align:start size:97% position:3%
And now it's just, I listened
to some hard partisans,

00:13:06.352 --> 00:13:08.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, I listen to
certain podcasts and so on.

00:13:08.487 --> 00:13:10.656 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's interesting and
it's sort of like a tickler,

00:13:10.656 --> 00:13:13.192 align:start size:84% position:16%
like this is what it's
like on this side,

00:13:13.192 --> 00:13:15.795
but I'm, I always
end up thinking,

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:17.496 align:start size:81% position:19%
I just don't wanna
be that person.

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:21.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just not at heart
this hard partisan person.

00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:24.303
I'm not, I wouldn't describe
myself as a moderate though,

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:26.705 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I have strong
points of view.

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:29.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, what I
believe, I really believe

00:13:29.008 --> 00:13:30.209
and I feel strongly about,

00:13:30.209 --> 00:13:32.711 align:start size:84% position:16%
but so I'm not kind
of wishy washy,

00:13:32.711 --> 00:13:35.815
but I also feel no
loyalty either side.

00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:37.917
I'm not, I'm certainly
not a loyal Democrat.

00:13:37.917 --> 00:13:39.318 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've been a
registered Republican,

00:13:39.318 --> 00:13:41.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I'm a registered
Independent now.

00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:43.756
I've been a registered
Democrat too, by the way.

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:46.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I just, I look at
these parties and I'm like,

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:48.828
yeah, you don't represent me,

00:13:48.828 --> 00:13:51.730
but you know, I'll take what
I believe in from both sides.

00:13:52.832 --> 00:13:55.234 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, and yet
everyone seems to have

00:13:55.234 --> 00:14:00.005
to make a political statement
about everything constantly.

00:14:00.005 --> 00:14:01.540
So if you were had to,

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:04.577
if you had to describe your
political beliefs right now,

00:14:04.577 --> 00:14:07.079
like what is that?

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.515
What are they?

00:14:09.515 --> 00:14:12.017 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I mean, I would
say I'm center-right

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:13.552
on a lot of issues.

00:14:13.552 --> 00:14:16.355
I'm center-left on
some other issues.

00:14:16.355 --> 00:14:18.924
I took a test online that
says like, what are you?

00:14:18.924 --> 00:14:21.827
You know, and when I, when I,

00:14:21.827 --> 00:14:24.196
yeah, and it said I was a
conservative Republican,

00:14:24.196 --> 00:14:26.565
and I was like, ah, and then I
had Doug, my husband take it,

00:14:26.565 --> 00:14:28.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it said, he's a
conservative Republican.

00:14:28.701 --> 00:14:30.236
And we're both Independents

00:14:30.236 --> 00:14:32.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have voted for
Democrats and Republicans,

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:36.108
you know, like all
throughout our lives.

00:14:36.108 --> 00:14:38.978 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I just think like the
country's moving so far left

00:14:38.978 --> 00:14:40.880
to some extent, like the,

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.782
the things that used to be
center-left or even center

00:14:43.782 --> 00:14:46.352 align:start size:81% position:19%
are now right,
established right.

00:14:47.486 --> 00:14:48.721 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I don't know
when that happened,

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:51.357
but I would still
vote for a Democrat

00:14:51.357 --> 00:14:53.025 align:start size:81% position:19%
if I saw the right
one, you know?

00:14:53.893 --> 00:14:55.394
And I don't know,

00:14:55.394 --> 00:14:57.529
I'm certainly not hard down
the party line Republican.

00:14:57.529 --> 00:14:58.764 align:start size:84% position:16%
There are a lot of
them who I don't like,

00:14:58.764 --> 00:14:59.932
and I voted against.

00:15:01.066 --> 00:15:02.701
- Yeah, so what was
it like for you,

00:15:02.701 --> 00:15:05.771
to sort of be someone that
was supposed to be talking

00:15:05.771 --> 00:15:08.574
about the news, but also for
a lot of the time you were,

00:15:08.574 --> 00:15:09.875
you were kind of making news.

00:15:09.875 --> 00:15:11.076
I mean, everyone knows the,

00:15:11.076 --> 00:15:14.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
what happened with
Trump and the debates,

00:15:15.381 --> 00:15:17.883 align:start size:88% position:13%
but that you sort of got
sucked into news too.

00:15:17.883 --> 00:15:21.754
And in the movie, there's
a line where Nicole Kidman

00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:23.422
as you basically
says that you know-

00:15:23.422 --> 00:15:24.990
- No, no, Charlize Theron

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:28.594
- Oh, sorry Charlize
Theron where she says,

00:15:28.594 --> 00:15:31.563
you know, that she, you,
basically saying, you know,

00:15:31.563 --> 00:15:33.999
you didn't wanna
be making the news.

00:15:33.999 --> 00:15:36.502 align:start size:84% position:16%
I assume that's pretty
much how you feel.

00:15:37.369 --> 00:15:38.904
- Yeah, I said,

00:15:38.904 --> 00:15:40.372
I'm not gonna be the story,
I don't wanna be the story.

00:15:40.372 --> 00:15:43.575 align:start size:88% position:13%
And, and I was the
story after that debate

00:15:43.575 --> 00:15:45.010
and I hated it.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:48.781 align:start position:0%
And I have hated being the
story every time it's happened.

00:15:48.781 --> 00:15:52.318 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, I see the
journalists as, as you know,

00:15:52.318 --> 00:15:55.254
on the sidelines, not
as players on the field

00:15:55.254 --> 00:15:58.223
and you know, Trump, to
some extent grabbed me

00:15:58.223 --> 00:16:01.593 align:start size:97% position:3%
and put me on the field and
the Roger Ailes thing did too.

00:16:01.593 --> 00:16:02.828
And then just, I don't know,

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:05.531
once you get well
known, you know,

00:16:05.531 --> 00:16:07.633
the sleazy media takes
a big interest in you

00:16:07.633 --> 00:16:09.068
and starts following you around.

00:16:09.068 --> 00:16:11.437 align:start size:88% position:13%
And they're not all
bad, some guys are good.

00:16:11.437 --> 00:16:14.540 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's actually a sweet
guy, right after I left NBC,

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:16.508
all these paparazzi were
outside of my apartment.

00:16:16.508 --> 00:16:19.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, couldn't
like leave without getting

00:16:19.745 --> 00:16:21.213
(imitates cameras clicking)

00:16:21.213 --> 00:16:23.682
And this one guy who was from
The Post, he got his shot.

00:16:23.682 --> 00:16:26.885
He's like, and then he goes,
this is such bullshit Megan,

00:16:26.885 --> 00:16:28.454
you can't say anything anymore.

00:16:29.888 --> 00:16:32.992 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like, there are real people
out there they're not all bad,

00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:36.462
but I don't like being
the topic of the news.

00:16:36.462 --> 00:16:39.431 align:start size:97% position:3%
I have asked myself many times
why that keeps happening.

00:16:39.431 --> 00:16:41.200
You know, I think,

00:16:42.634 --> 00:16:45.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think people aren't used
to seeing like somebody

00:16:45.871 --> 00:16:47.573
they can't figure out,

00:16:47.573 --> 00:16:51.243
somebody who's sort of
unapologetically strong,

00:16:51.243 --> 00:16:53.912
especially, especially a
woman, we're out there,

00:16:53.912 --> 00:16:56.648
but like, it's not that common.

00:16:56.648 --> 00:17:00.252 align:start size:84% position:16%
And a woman who
doesn't mind fighting.

00:17:00.252 --> 00:17:03.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
Right, like it's like,
what, what, what you doing?

00:17:03.822 --> 00:17:05.657
But you know that I'm
feudalistic by nature.

00:17:05.657 --> 00:17:08.160
And I think it, it
may be exciting.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:11.964
It may be upsetting, you
know, maybe alienating,

00:17:11.964 --> 00:17:15.667 align:start size:88% position:13%
but for whatever reason,
it's attractive news.

00:17:15.667 --> 00:17:18.303 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, it's funny to me
because as you're getting back

00:17:18.303 --> 00:17:20.272 align:start size:84% position:16%
into the fray, like,
it's so obvious,

00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:23.275 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's gonna be a moment
like within a couple of months

00:17:23.275 --> 00:17:25.177
where something's gonna happen,

00:17:25.177 --> 00:17:27.546 align:start position:0%
like you're gonna say
something or one of your guests

00:17:27.546 --> 00:17:29.014
is gonna say, sorry, psych.

00:17:29.014 --> 00:17:31.383 align:start size:97% position:3%
And you're gonna be like,
"Ugh, why did I get back in?"

00:17:31.383 --> 00:17:33.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then, but then an
hour later you'll be like,

00:17:33.252 --> 00:17:34.920 align:start size:81% position:19%
this is exactly
why I got back in.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.189
Like, that's just a negotiation.

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:39.391
- I don't think that's
going to happen to me.

00:17:39.391 --> 00:17:40.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I do think they're
gonna come after me,

00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:42.261
you know, knives out,

00:17:42.261 --> 00:17:45.697
but I'm just so used to being
attacked for everything I say,

00:17:45.697 --> 00:17:47.332
it's like, at this
point, I'm like,

00:17:47.332 --> 00:17:48.834 align:start size:81% position:19%
"All right, you
know, what do you,

00:17:48.834 --> 00:17:50.602 align:start size:97% position:3%
what are you gonna do, are you
gonna call me a mean name?"

00:17:50.602 --> 00:17:52.104
What would that feel like?

00:17:52.104 --> 00:17:53.605
What would it feel like to
see myself called something

00:17:53.605 --> 00:17:56.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
horrible in every
newspaper in the country?

00:17:56.141 --> 00:17:57.776
Oh, wait, I've done that.

00:17:57.776 --> 00:18:00.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
In a way it's sort of
empowering 'cause it's like,

00:18:00.379 --> 00:18:02.047
they, they took their best shot.

00:18:02.047 --> 00:18:04.483
I'm here, I'm well, I'm happy.

00:18:04.483 --> 00:18:07.886 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm about to launch something
that I'm really into.

00:18:07.886 --> 00:18:11.824
And for once Dave, like,
they can't get rid of me.

00:18:11.824 --> 00:18:13.325
They can't get rid
of me, you know?

00:18:13.325 --> 00:18:16.995
Like even if every sponsor
I have is like, "We're out!"

00:18:16.995 --> 00:18:18.564 align:start size:88% position:13%
Then I'll do
subscription, you know,

00:18:18.564 --> 00:18:21.266
the relationship will be
